From b8bec7cff2e6778fe6709dee3f35c4380077e152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite Patch <noreply@auralite.local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] HOME H0: /home directory and the user database

HOME_PLAN.md phase H0: the tree gets a home directory and a user database,
and the shell stops pretending.

- kernel/fs/home.{c,h} (new): /home mounts as its own tmpfs volume (the
  mount-point construction /documents proved: a symlink resolves on lookup
  but not on create, so open(O_CREAT) fails EROFS), with its own 256-file
  table so scratch traffic cannot evict a user's file. /etc/passwd from the
  initrd is parsed once at boot into a 16-record table; malformed lines are
  REFUSED and counted rather than truncated into a wrong home; 5-field
  records are malformed, 6-field default the shell. The boot bring-up
  creates each home and proves the first writable.
- Durability is stated, not pretended: storage=tmpfs (volatile: HOME_PLAN
  H4 makes it durable).
- SYS_GETPWENT (546) / SYS_GETHOME (547): buffers validated with
  validate_user_range(); records returned in the /etc/passwd grammar so
  libc parses one format.
- lib/libc/src/pwd.c rewritten from the stub: getpwuid/getpwnam/getpwent/
  setpwent/endpwent/getpwuid_r, with the pre-H0 root answer kept as an
  explicit fallback when the table is empty.
- The shell stops pretending: pwd prints getcwd() (it was a constant '/'),
  cd [dir] exists (bare cd goes home), ~ expands in arguments but not when
  quoted, HOME/USER exported from ONE getpwuid(getuid()) -- the first draft
  called it three times inside one ternary and shipped USER= empty.
- ls / shows the mount table: vfs_readdir() unions in the mount points that
  live directly under the listed path, deduped against the backing listing;
  ls /home needed vol_of_vnode() to know home_vol (the identical omission
  OF2's closure fixed for doc_vol).
- /etc/passwd ships two records; root's home is /home/root, NOT /root --
  /root lives on the read-only initrd (EROFS on the first save) and the
  shell runs as uid 0.
- Tests: tests/unit/test_home_passwd.c compiles the SHIPPED parser on the
  host (26 grammar checks) plus a mutation lane that removes the
  default-shell rule and REQUIRES exit 1; tests/integration/cases/
  test_home.sh (registered in ALL_CASES, fs shard) proves it end to end in
  QEMU: 13/13.
- Ratchets moved in the same change: check_width_sweep's (uint64_t)
  counter did not move (offsets carried as size_t); check_parity_claims
  FS_FILE_COUNT 26 -> 27 and home.c compiles at rv64/a64/i386 with
  -Wshorten-64-to-32 (which caught three long/int64_t conversions); SH8's
  in-guest source pin 152 -> 153 in all four places; residue ledger
  RES-65 + pins.

Docs: docs/plans/HOME_PLAN.md (new), CHANGELOG.md, docs/filesystem.md,
docs/status.md, docs/residue_ledger.md, docs/plans/RESIDUE3_PLAN.md.

Gates: make test-unit 259/259 exit 0; test_home 13/13; test_home_passwd
26/26 + mutation lane red as required; make iso boots.
